---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import DebtPayoffLab from "../../components/DebtPayoffLab.tsx";
import "../../styles/simtool.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Debt Payoff: Avalanche vs. Snowball"
  description="Compare the two debt-payoff strategies on your own debts: avalanche (highest rate first) saves the most interest, snowball (smallest balance first) builds momentum. See months to debt-free, total interest, and a refinance flag for high rates."
>
  <section class="container wl-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Personal Finance · Interactive Tool</p>
    <h1>Debt payoff: avalanche vs. snowball</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      High-interest debt is a guaranteed negative return — paying off a 22% card
      beats any bet the market offers. But <em>which</em> debt do you attack first?
      The two popular answers, <strong>avalanche</strong> and
      <strong>snowball</strong>, split the difference between math and momentum.
      Enter your debts and see how each plays out for you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-host">
    <DebtPayoffLab client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-explainer">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The two strategies</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Avalanche — highest interest rate first.</strong> You pay the
          minimum on everything, then throw every spare dollar at your
          <em>highest-APR</em> debt until it's gone, then the next-highest, and so
          on. This mathematically minimizes the interest you pay and usually clears
          everything soonest. It's the optimal choice on paper.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Snowball — smallest balance first.</strong> Same minimums, but you
          target your <em>smallest balance</em> first, regardless of rate. You clear
          a whole debt quickly, which frees its payment and — more importantly —
          gives you a visible win. For a lot of people, that momentum is what keeps
          them going.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        As each debt is cleared, its old minimum payment rolls into the pile
        attacking the next one — the "snowball" that gives the method its name (both
        strategies do this). The best strategy is usually avalanche on the
        spreadsheet and snowball in real life; if the interest difference is small,
        the one you'll actually stick with wins.
      </p>
      <h2>When a rate is just too high</h2>
      <p>
        Before you grind a balance down, it's worth asking whether the rate itself
        can be lowered. If you enter an APR well above what's typical for that kind
        of debt, the tool flags it and suggests where refinancing, a balance
        transfer, or consolidation might help — with the usual caveats that those
        moves have costs and aren't always worth it. Educational only, not advice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pf-related">
    <h2 class="pf-related-heading">Keep exploring</h2>
    <ul class="grid grid--2 pf-related-grid">
      <li>
        <a href="/personal-finance" class="card">
          <h3>More personal-finance tools</h3>
          <p>Budgeting, emergency funds, savings goals, and rent vs. buy.</p>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/tools/compound-growth" class="card">
          <h3>Debt is compounding in reverse</h3>
          <p>
            The Growth tool shows the same math that builds wealth working against
            you when you borrow.
          </p>
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wl-intro {
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md);
    max-width: var(--measure-wide);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .wl-explainer {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .pf-related {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }
  .pf-related-heading {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-xs);
    border-bottom: var(--border);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }
  .pf-related-grid {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .pf-related-grid a.card {
    height: 100%;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    display: block;
  }
  .pf-related-grid h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }
  .pf-related-grid p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
</style>

<style is:global>
  /* Shared result-card styles (also used by other sim tools). */
  .ss-headline {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-accent);
  }
  .ss-headline-label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .ss-headline-value {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .ss-headline-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }

  /* Debt table */
  .dp-debts {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .dp-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(6rem, 1.3fr) minmax(6.5rem, 1fr) 7rem 5rem 6.5rem 1.7rem;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    align-items: center;
    min-width: 33rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .dp-head {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }
  .dp-in {
    width: 100%;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    padding: 0.35rem 0.45rem;
    border: var(--border);
    border-radius: 7px;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
  .dp-in:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    outline-offset: 1px;
  }
  .dp-money,
  .dp-pct {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .dp-money .dp-in,
  .dp-pct .dp-in {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .dp-del {
    width: 1.7rem;
    height: 1.7rem;
    border: var(--border);
    border-radius: 7px;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .dp-del:hover:not(:disabled) {
    border-color: var(--color-error);
    color: var(--color-error);
  }
  .dp-del:disabled {
    opacity: 0.35;
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }
  .dp-add {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px dashed var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 7px;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.7rem;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .dp-add:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  /* Refinance callouts */
  .dp-refis {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .dp-refi {
    padding: 0.6rem 0.85rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-warn);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-warn) 10%, transparent);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .dp-refi strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
  .dp-refi-foot {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Strategy comparison */
  .dp-compare {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }
  .dp-strat {
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .dp-strat--win {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
  }
  .dp-strat h4 {
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .dp-strat h4 span {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .dp-strat dl {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.3rem;
  }
  .dp-strat dl > div {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .dp-strat dt {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .dp-strat dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
